## Claim
Text: "Hunter Biden, son of US President Joe Biden has died."
Claim date: October 25, 2020
Claim origin: https://web.archive.org/web/20210116153238/https://media.thedonald.win/post/H3A2atAb.png

## Initial Q&A
### Is Hunter Biden biologically and factually the son of Joe Biden, the 46th President of the United States?
Answer: Yes, according to the source, Hunter Biden is factually Joe Biden's son. The PBS article explicitly refers to "Joe Biden's son Hunter" multiple times, and Hunter Biden himself is quoted referencing "my father" in the context of his father's political career, confirming the biological and factual relationship.

Source URL: https://www.pbs.org/newshour/politics/hunter-biden-says-he-did-not-have-an-ethical-lapse

### Was Joe Biden serving as the President of the United States on October 25, 2020?
Answer: No, Joe Biden was not serving as the President of the United States on October 25, 2020. According to the source, Biden "became the 46th president of the United States on January 20, 2021." On October 25, 2020, Biden was still a presidential candidate, and Donald Trump was the sitting president, as evidenced by the reference to a presidential debate held on October 22, 2020, between Biden and "President Trump."

Source URL: https://www.history.com/topics/us-presidents/joe-biden

### Is Hunter Biden alive as of the current date, or has he died at any point in time?
Answer: Hunter Biden is alive. According to USA Today's fact check, "There is no evidence to support [the claim that he died], and it appears to be a hoax that originated on 4chan." The article notes that as of October 2020, "Hunter Biden...lives in Los Angeles" and was described as "a recovering drug addict," with the death rumors being definitively debunked by multiple fact-checking organizations including Lead Stories and Heavy.

Source URL: https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/factcheck/2020/10/27/fact-check-rumors-hunter-biden-dead-4-chan-hoax/3754066001/

### Did any major, reputable news outlets (such as the New York Times, Washington Post, Reuters, or AP) report the death of Hunter Biden in or around October 2020?
Answer: No, no major, reputable news outlets reported the death of Hunter Biden in or around October 2020. According to the USA Today fact check, the claim was a hoax originating from a 4chan post on October 25, 2020, and was debunked by fact-checkers including Lead Stories and Heavy. On the contrary, major outlets like the Associated Press reported on Joe Biden's campaign activities during that period (attending church on October 25, campaigning in Pennsylvania on October 26, and heading to Georgia on October 27), which would have been impossible if Hunter had actually died and Joe were rushing to a hospital as the hoax claimed.

Source URL: https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/factcheck/2020/10/27/fact-check-rumors-hunter-biden-dead-4-chan-hoax/3754066001/

### Are there any official death records, obituaries, or funeral reports for Hunter Biden associated with the year 2020?
Answer: No. According to the USA Today fact check, "There is no proof to support the claim that Hunter Biden is dead" and "There is no evidence to support it, and it appears to be a hoax that originated on 4chan." Multiple fact-checking organizations (USA Today, Lead Stories, and Heavy) concluded that the death rumors were false, and no official death records, obituaries, or funeral reports for Hunter Biden exist for 2020.

Source URL: https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/factcheck/2020/10/27/fact-check-rumors-hunter-biden-dead-4-chan-hoax/3754066001/

### Were there any fact-checking organizations that investigated and debunked a claim about Hunter Biden's death circulating in October 2020?
Answer: Yes, multiple fact-checking organizations investigated and debunked the claim that Hunter Biden had died. USA TODAY published a fact check on October 27, 2020, labeling the claim as FALSE, and noted that "Both Lead Stories and Heavy also concluded that the claim is false." Specifically, "Lead Stories, Oct. 26, Fact Check: NO Evidence That Hunter Biden Is Dead" and "Heavy, Oct. 26, Hunter Biden Is Not Dead: Overdose Story Is a 4chan Death Hoax."

Source URL: https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/factcheck/2020/10/27/fact-check-rumors-hunter-biden-dead-4-chan-hoax/3754066001/

### If Hunter Biden did not die, what is the likely motivation or origin behind the false claim that he had died as of October 25, 2020?
Answer: Based on the search result, the false claim about Hunter Biden's death as of October 25, 2020 likely originated as part of the broader proliferation of conspiracy theories during the 2020 presidential election cycle, particularly those aimed at damaging the Biden campaign. The article notes that "there has been a proliferation of conspiracy theories during the 2020 election cycle" and that baseless claims often emerged from "niche online communities, including QAnon," as well as pro-Trump forums like TheDonald.win (where the claim originated). Given the timing—just 15 days before the election—the death claim was likely manufactured to spread misinformation, generate engagement, and fuel anti-Biden narratives alongside other unfounded theories about Hunter Biden's laptop and alleged criminal activity, all of which were part of a coordinated effort to influence the election outcome in Trump's favor.

Source URL: https://www.newsweek.com/hunter-biden-laptop-qanon-conspiracy-theories-2020-election-1540173

## Final Judgement
## Summary of Key Findings

The evidence from the fact-check is clear and comprehensive. Hunter Biden is confirmed to be alive, and the claim that he died was thoroughly debunked as a hoax originating from a 4chan post on October 25, 2020. Multiple reputable fact-checking organizations (USA Today, Lead Stories, and Heavy) investigated and labeled the claim as FALSE. No major news outlets reported his death, no official death records or obituaries exist, and Joe Biden's campaign activities during that period (attending church, campaigning in Pennsylvania and Georgia) would have been impossible if he were rushing to be with a dying son. Additionally, while the claim refers to Joe Biden as "US President," he was not yet president on October 25, 2020—he was a presidential candidate, as he didn't take office until January 20, 2021.

## Missing Information

No further information is needed. The evidence is conclusive and unambiguous.

## Conclusion

The claim that "Hunter Biden, son of US President Joe Biden has died" is definitively refuted by the evidence. Hunter Biden is alive, the death rumors were a debunked hoax from 4chan, and no credible source reported his death. Furthermore, the claim incorrectly describes Joe Biden as "US President" when, as of the claim date of October 25, 2020, he had not yet taken office.

