### Justification
The claim that Hunter Biden died is definitively false. Hunter Biden is alive, and the death rumors were a hoax originating from a [4chan post on October 25, 2020](https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/factcheck/2020/10/27/fact-check-rumors-hunter-biden-dead-4-chan-hoax/3754066001/), debunked by multiple fact-checking organizations including [USA Today](https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/factcheck/2020/10/27/fact-check-rumors-hunter-biden-dead-4-chan-hoax/3754066001/), [Lead Stories](https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/factcheck/2020/10/27/fact-check-rumors-hunter-biden-dead-4-chan-hoax/3754066001/), and [Heavy](https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/factcheck/2020/10/27/fact-check-rumors-hunter-biden-dead-4-chan-hoax/3754066001/). No major news outlets reported his death, no official death records or obituaries exist, and Joe Biden's active campaign schedule during that period (attending church, campaigning in Pennsylvania and Georgia) contradicts the claim. Additionally, the claim incorrectly identifies Joe Biden as "US President," when he was still a presidential candidate on October 25, 2020, not taking office until [January 20, 2021](https://www.history.com/topics/us-presidents/joe-biden). The hoax was part of a broader wave of [conspiracy theories during the 2020 election cycle](https://www.newsweek.com/hunter-biden-laptop-qanon-conspiracy-theories-2020-election-1540173) aimed at damaging the Biden campaign.